<title>USA: Biodynamics hurt by Japan dura mater ban.</title>
<headline>Biodynamics hurt by Japan dura mater ban.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biodynamics International Inc said Friday that revenues from Japan will be hurt by the country's ban of all uses of dura mater, a human brain tissue.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the Japanese Ministry of Health banned all uses of human dura mater, including the company's Tutoplast dura mater, in response to a recommendation from the United Nations World Health Organization.</p>
<p>The ban does not include other human tissues processed by Biodynamics and distributed in Japan.</p>
<p>Biodynamics said it lodge a strong protest with WHO and ask that their statement be revised to reflect the record of safety of its human dura mater tissue.</p>
<p>The company said it will also request reinstatement of Tutoplast dura mater by the Japanese Ministry of Health.</p>
</text>
